# Build-context filter for the two frontend images, which build from the
# REPOSITORY ROOT (see octbase-frontend/Containerfile) because the SPAs import
# the @octbase/shared workspace package from outside their own directories.
#
# A root context would otherwise stream the whole working tree — including the
# local Postgres data directory, which is owned by the container's UID and is
# not even readable here. Deny everything, then re-admit exactly what the two
# Containerfiles COPY.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!octbase-shared
!octbase-frontend
!octbase-mobile
# Both vite.config.js files import their build plugins from outside their own
# directory, so the build stage cannot run without them — the Vite config fails
# to LOAD, before it compiles anything. Admitted by pattern rather than by name:
# this is a deny-all list, so a plugin added later is invisible to the image
# while every host build stays green, and the error it produces
# ("Could not resolve '../scripts/…' in vite.config.js") points at the config,
# not at this file. That is exactly how adding vite-strip-html-comments.mjs
# broke both image builds on 2026-08-01.
#   vite-hash-classic-assets  hashes the classic scripts the bundler leaves
#                             alone (37b stage 5)
#   vite-strip-html-comments  drops HTML comments from the built pages
# Still nothing else from scripts/: the rest is repo tooling, not part of an image.
!scripts/vite-*.mjs

# ...minus the parts of those trees an image must never carry: build output
# (the image builds its own), dependencies (installed by `npm ci` inside), and
# the dev-only test layer.
octbase-*/dist
octbase-*/dist-standalone
octbase-*/tests
**/node_modules
**/*.test.js
octbase-frontend/js/testutil.js
